+ * finger and grounding, and drifts from session to session. It is a
+ * running MEDIAN of moving, unpressed touches (a fixed-rate step toward
+ * each sample), ignoring samples already well above it. A plain average
+ * drifted upward in testing, because a press-and-drag is a moving, firm
+ * finger before the press registers, and each one raised the threshold
+ * until selections stopped registering. */
